column5:
Removed the semicolon after PyObject_HEAD

While empty `struct-declaration`s are apparently fine for some
compilers, MSVC++ 9 does not accept it. Since PyObject_HEAD
expands to multiple `struct-declaration`s (including terminating
semicolon), code like

    struct {
        PyObject_HEAD;
        int some_field;
        // ...
    }

would expand to a struct with an "empty" `struct-declaration`.

Added ability to use strings for interval creation,

e.g.
@interval("0.1", "0.2")

Proper display for Interval{Rational{T}} (#177)

* Proper display for Interval{Rational{T}}

* Add 0.5 explicitly to travis

Added ability to use strings for interval creation,

e.g.
@interval("0.1", "0.2")

return empty footprint if partly outside of the map (#272)

* return empty footprint if partly outside of the map
* Adapt srvs comments to reflect that OUTSIDE means partially outside
